OL,3,CThousands of 999 calls across West
OL,4,CMidlands after 'apocalyptic' fires
OL,6,FElsewhere in the region, smoke from
OL,7,Fnearby wildfires forced the closure of
OL,8,Fthe M6 northbound between junctions
OL,9,Ffive and six ` causing more than two
OL,10,Fhours of delays.
OL,12,FExplaining the closure, National
OL,13,FHighways West Midlands said in a
OL,14,Fstatement: "The fire keeps igniting.
OL,15,FFire commander at the scene not happy
OL,16,Ffor M6 to be reopened until fire fully
OL,17,Fextinguished."
OL,19,FThe motorway later reopened but
OL,20,Fmotorists continued to face six miles
OL,21,Fof congestion.
OL,26,@vD@LOUyD@NO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
